WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.937
Zero-shot prompting asks the model to perform a task without worked examples.

00:00:04.937 --> 00:00:11.172
Strong instruction models can handle many common tasks this way, especially when the request, constraints,

00:00:11.172 --> 00:00:14.362
and output format are clear.

00:00:14.362 --> 00:00:18.317
It is usually the simplest baseline to try first.

00:00:18.317 --> 00:00:23.462
Always try a simple zero-shot baseline before adding many examples.

00:00:23.462 --> 00:00:27.216
You may find that the model already handles the task well enough.
